<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Contract baseline for signal, plan and decision routes</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies code files (.cs tests under tests/**; root CLAUDE.md §8 runs code-review and adr-check on tests/** tasks)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Test authoring over existing in-process route harnesses (SignalReadRouteTests, DecisionCommitServiceTests) with a closed list of routes and codes</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>testing, integration-test, bff-api, api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Before any extraction changes the code behind them, record the current REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision — success and every reason code each can return today — as byte-level golden contract tests (FR-09 guard for 012–017).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core integration testing and HTTP contract testing.</role>
  <goal>tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/ holds golden contract tests and files for the four routes that pass on the unchanged code, plus an inventory of every reason code and its HTTP status in notes/contract-baseline.md.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-09 (REST byte-for-byte unchanged against recorded contract tests) and the plan's critical path: 011 must precede 017, 013 and 014. No dedicated decision-plan route test exists today (pipeline Step 2 finding).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/SignalRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/Baselines/ (one golden JSON per case)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/contract-baseline.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests/Signals/SignalReadRouteTests.cs (in-process route harness)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/DecisionCommitServiceTests.cs and DecisionCommitServiceTests.InvoiceReview.cs (fixture shapes)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/StatedCaller.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs (DecisionCommitReasons constants L199-245)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs (ToHttp L61), SignalReadEndpoints.cs (L46, L85), DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (L138, L149, L251-345)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisite task; startable in Wave 1.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">This task changes no file under src/; the tests run against the code as it is at the task's start commit (recorded in notes/contract-baseline.md).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Each baseline compares status code, Content-Type and the response body bytes; the only normalised values are fields that change per run (timestamps, trace ids, correlation ids, generated ids), each named in one list in the test file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every reason code each route can return today gets one baseline case, including ontology.decision.decided_in_invoice_review (409), the uniform 404, 401 for an anonymous call and the worklist's 503 too_many_signals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>tests/integration/contract/README.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/integration-tests.md</file>
      <file>.claude/FAILURE-MODES.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory reason codes: DecisionCommitReasons (DecisionCommitService.cs L199-245) plus every code SignalReadEndpoints and DecisionPlanEndpoints can emit; map each to the HTTP status its endpoint returns; write the table to notes/contract-baseline.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Build the golden-file harness on the existing in-process route harness: request → status, Content-Type, normalised body bytes → compare with Baselines/{case}.json; a missing golden file fails the test (no auto-write in CI).</step>
    <step order="3">Add one case per route success and per reachable reason code; reuse the #2580 fixture shapes for the billing 409.</step>
    <step order="4">Generate the golden files once from the unchanged code, review them by eye, commit them.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof: change one character of a ProblemDetails title in DecisionCommitEndpoints.ToHttp locally, confirm the relevant baseline fails, restore the code.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the contract suite and the existing Signals suites.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a reason code cannot be reached through the route harness without a production change, STOP and list it in notes/contract-baseline.md as 'not baselined' with the reason, rather than changing src/.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a route's response varies between runs beyond the named volatile fields, STOP and escalate (a nondeterministic contract cannot be frozen).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests/Signals/SignalReadRouteTests.cs asserts worklist behaviour but not response bytes; no decision-plan route test exists; no golden-file contract test exists for these routes (grep -rln decision-plan tests/integration/contract returns nothing).</existing>
    <extension>No: the existing tests assert behaviour, not bytes, and FR-09 needs a byte-level freeze recorded before the refactor; the new file reuses their harness.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Tasks 012–017 could change a REST response without any test failing, breaking the Console's worklist and wizard silently (FR-09, success criterion 6).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/SignalRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/Baselines/</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/contract-baseline.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Baseline cases exist for the success response of each of the four routes and for every reachable reason code, including 409 ontology.decision.decided_in_invoice_review, the uniform 404, 401 anonymous and 503 too_many_signals.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All baseline tests pass on the unchanged code; the start commit SHA is recorded in notes/contract-baseline.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The normalisation list in the test file names only per-run volatile fields.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the seeding proof (one changed ProblemDetails character) makes the relevant baseline fail; the code is restored and the suite is green again.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a missing golden file fails the test instead of writing a new file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/ is changed by this task (git diff --stat evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/contract-baseline.md lists every reason code with route, HTTP status and baseline case name (017 uses it for its MCP mapping tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>FAILURE-MODES AP-9: later tasks must never edit a golden file to make a refactor pass; a needed change is an escalation. G-12: run without --no-build.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
